Let $\hbar_{J,g}$ be the smaller of the constants~$\hbar_{J,g}$ in Corollaries~ef{LowEner_crl} and~ef{CylEner_crl}. Let $u_i$, $u$, and~$\mathfrak m$ be as in the statement of the corollary.\ 
oindent ef{fmLowBnd_it} For each $i\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+$, let $$M_i=\max_{\ov{B_{1/2}}} ig|	extnormal{d}_zu_i ig|_g\in\mathbb R^+$$ and $z_i\!\in\!\ov{B_{1/2}}$ be such that $|	extnormal{d}_{z_i}u_i|_g\!=\!M_i$. Since $M_i\!\longrightarrow\!\infty$ as $i\!\longrightarrow\!\infty$ and $u_i$ converges uniformly in the $C^{\infty}$-topology on compact subsets of~$B_1^*$ to~$u$, $z_i\!\longrightarrow\!0$. For $i\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+$ such that $|z_i|\!+\!1/\sqrt{M_i}\!<\!1/2$, define $$v_i\!:B_{\sqrt{M_i}}\longrightarrow X, \qquad v_i(z)=u_i ig(z_i\!+\!z/M_i ig).$$ Thus, $v_i$ is a $J$-holomorphic map with \BE{EnerPres2_e3}\sup ig|	extnormal{d} v_i ig|_g= ig|	extnormal{d}_0v_i ig|_g=1, \qquad E_g(v_i)=E_g ig(u_i;B_{1/\sqrt{M_i}}(z_i) ig)\le E_g ig(u_i;B_{|z_i|+1/\sqrt{M_i}} ig)\,.\end{equation} By the first statement in~(ef{EnerPres2_e3}) and the ellipticity of the $ ar\partial$-operator, a subsequence of~$v_i$ converges uniformly in the $C^{\infty}$-topology on compact subsets of~$\mathbb{C}$ to a non-constant $J$-holomorphic map \hbox{$v\!:\mathbb{C}\!\longrightarrow\!X$}. By the second statement in~(ef{EnerPres2_e3}) and Lemma~ef{EnerPres1_lmm}ef{deEner_it}, \BE{EnerPres2_e5} E_g(v) \le \limsup_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g ig(u_i;B_{1/\sqrt{M_i}}(z_i) ig) \le \lim_{\delta\longrightarrow0}\lim_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g ig(u_i;B_{\delta} ig)=\mathfrak m.\end{equation} By Proposition~ef{RemSing_prp}, $v$ thus extends to a $J$-holomorphic map $\wt{v}\!:\mathbb{P}^1\!\longrightarrow\!X$. By Corollary~ef{LowEner_crl}, $$E_g(v)=E_g(\wt{v})\ge \hbar_{J,g}\,.$$ Combining this with~(ef{EnerPres2_e5}), we obtain the first claim.\ 
oindent ef{noLoss_it} By the first two statements in Lemma~ef{EnerPres1_lmm} and~(ef{fmdfn_e}), \BE{noLoss_e2} \lim_{\delta\longrightarrow0}\lim_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g ig(u_i;B_{\delta}(z_i) ig)= \lim_{\delta\longrightarrow0}\mathfrak m(\delta)=\mathfrak m.\end{equation} After passing to a subsequence of~$u_i$, we can thus assume that there exists a sequence $\delta_i\!\longrightarrow\!0$ such~that \BE{noLoss_e3} \lim_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g(u_i;B_{\delta_i}(z_i))=\mathfrak m.\end{equation} Since $\delta_i\!\longrightarrow\!0$, (ef{noLoss_e2}) and (ef{noLoss_e3}) imply that \BE{noLoss_e5}\lim_{R\longrightarrow\infty}\lim_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g(u_i;B_{R\delta_i}(z_i))=\mathfrak m.\end{equation} \vspace{.1in} 
oindent Suppose $\mu\!\in\!(\mathfrak m\!-\!\hbar_{J,g},\mathfrak m)$. By (ef{noLoss_e5}) and the definition of~$\delta_i(\mu)$, $$ \lim_{R\longrightarrow\infty}\lim_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g ig(u;B_{R\delta_i}(z_i)\!-\!B_{\delta_i(\mu)}(z_i) ig) =\mathfrak m\!-\!\mu<\hbar_{J,g}\,.$$ Thus, Corollary~ef{CylEner_crl} applies with $(R,T)$ replaced by $( rac12\ln(R\delta_i/\delta_i(\mu)),\ln R)$ and $u$ replaced by the $J$-holomorphic~map $$v\!: (-R,R)\!	imes\!S^1\longrightarrow X,\qquad v ig(r,	extnormal{e}^{\mathfrak i	heta} ig)=u ig(z_i\!+\!\sqrt{R\delta_i\delta_i(\mu)}\,	extnormal{e}^{r+\mathfrak i	heta} ig).$$ By the first statement of Corollary~ef{CylEner_crl}, $$E_g ig(u;B_{\delta_i}(z_i) ig)-E_g ig(u;B_{R\delta_i(\mu)}(z_i) ig)= E_g ig(u;B_{\delta_i}(z_i)\!-\!B_{R\delta_i(\mu)}(z_i) ig)\le  rac{C_{J,g}}{R}E_g(u)$$ for all $i$ sufficiently large (depending on~$R$); see Figure~ef{CylEner_fig}. Combining this with (ef{noLoss_e3}), we obtain~(ef{noEloss_e1}).\  egin{figure}  egin{pspicture}(3,-.3)(9,2.7) \psset{unit=.3cm} \psline[linewidth=.06](56,7)(20,7) \psline[linewidth=.06](56,1)(20,1) \psarc[linewidth=.04](59,4){4.24}{135}{225} \psarc[linewidth=.04,linestyle=dotted](53,4){4.24}{-45}{45} \psarc[linewidth=.04](48,4){4.24}{135}{225} \psarc[linewidth=.04,linestyle=dotted](42,4){4.24}{-45}{45} \psarc[linewidth=.04](34,4){4.24}{135}{225} \psarc[linewidth=.04,linestyle=dotted](28,4){4.24}{-45}{45} \psarc[linewidth=.04](23,4){4.24}{135}{225} \psarc[linewidth=.04,linestyle=dotted](17,4){4.24}{-45}{45} put(56,7.8){$\mathfrak m$}put(56,0){\sm{$\ln\delta_i\!+\!\ln R$}} put(45.2,7.8){$\mathfrak m$}put(45,0){\sm{$\ln\delta_i$}} put(20.2,7.8){$\mu$}put(20,0){\sm{$\ln\delta_i(\mu)$}} put(31.3,8){$\mu^*$}put(31,0){\sm{$\delta_i(\mu)\!+\!\ln R$}} put(38,4.5){\small{disappearing}}put(38,3){\small{energy}} \end{pspicture} \caption{Illustration for the proof of~(ef{noEloss_e1})} \end{figure} 
oindent It remains to establish~(ef{noEloss_e2}). By~(ef{EnerPres1Elim_e}), for all $R\!>\!0$ and sufficiently small $\delta\!>\!0$ (depending on~$R$) there exists $i(R,\delta)\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+$ such~that $$E_g ig(u_i;B_{R\delta}(z_i)\!-\!B_{\delta_i(\mu)}(z_i) ig)<\hbar_{J,g} \qquad orall~i>i(R,\delta).$$ Thus, Corollary~ef{CylEner_crl} applies with $(R,T)$ replaced by $( rac12\ln(R\delta/\delta_i(\mu)),\ln R)$ and $u$ replaced by the $J$-holomorphic~map $$v\!: (-R,R)\!	imes\!S^1\longrightarrow X,\qquad v ig(r,	extnormal{e}^{\mathfrak i	heta} ig)=u ig(z_i\!+\!\sqrt{R\delta\delta_i(\mu)}\,	extnormal{e}^{r+\mathfrak i	heta} ig).$$ By the second statement of Corollary~ef{CylEner_crl}, $$	extnormal{diam}_g ig(u_i(B_{\delta}(z_i)\!-\!B_{R\delta_i(\mu)}(z_i)) ig) \le  rac{C_{J,g}}{\sqrt{R}}\hbar_{J,g} \qquad orall~i>i(R,\delta).$$ This gives~(ef{noEloss_e2}).

Let $\hbar_{J,g}$ be the minimal value of the function provided by Proposition~ef{PtBnd_prp}. For $E\!\in\!\mathbb R^+$, let $N(E)\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^{\ge0}$ be the smallest integer such that $E\!\le\!N(E)\hbar_{J,g}$.\ 
oindent Let $\Sigma$, $S_0$, $u_i$, and $E$ be as in the statement of the lemma and $N\!=\!N(E)\!+\!|S_0|$. Fix a Riemannian metric~$g_{\Sigma}$ on~$\Sigma$. For $z\!\in\!\Sigma$ and $\delta\!\in\!\Sigma$, let $B_{\delta}(z)\!\subset\!\Sigma$ denote the ball of radius~$\delta$ around~$z$. By Proposition~ef{PtBnd_prp}, there exists $C\!\in\!\mathbb R^+$ with the following property. If $u\!:\Sigma\!\longrightarrow\!X$ is a $J$-holomorphic map, $z\!\in\!\Sigma$, and $\delta\!\in\!\mathbb R^+$, then \BE{EnerPres3_e3} E_g ig(u;B_{\delta}(z) ig)<\hbar_{J,g} \qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad  ig|	extnormal{d}_zu ig|_g\le C/\delta^2\,.\end{equation} \vspace{.1in} 
oindent For every pair $i,j\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+$, let $\{z_{ij}^k\}_{k=1}^N$ be a subset of points of~$\Sigma$ containing~$S_0$ such~that \BE{EnerPres3_e5} z\in \Sigma_{ij}^*\equiv\Sigma\!-\! igcup_{k=1}^N\!B_{2/j} ig(z_{ij}^k ig) \qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad E_g ig(u_i;B_{1/j}(z)\!\cap\!U_i ig)<\hbar_{J,g}\,.\end{equation} By~(ef{EnerPres3_e3}) and~(ef{EnerPres3_e5}), \BE{EnerPres3_e7}  ig|	extnormal{d}_zu_i ig|_g\le Cj^2 \qquad orall\,z\!\in\!\Sigma_{ij}^* ~\hbox{s.t.}~B_{1/j}(z)\!\subset\!U_i\,.\end{equation} \vspace{.1in} 
oindent After passing to a subsequence of~$\{u_i\}$, we can assume that the sequence $E_g(u_i)$ converges to~$E$ and that the sequence $\{z_{ij}^k\}_{i\in{\mathbb Z}^+}$ converges to some $z_j^k\!\in\!\Sigma$ for every $k\!=\!1,\ldots,N$ and $j\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+$. Along with~(ef{EnerPres3_e7}) and the first two assumptions in~(ef{EnerPres3_e}), this implies that \BE{EnerPres3_e9} \limsup_{i\longrightarrow\infty} ig|	extnormal{d}_zu_i ig|_g\le Cj^2 \qquad orall\,z\in\Sigma_{ij}^*\,.\end{equation} After passing to another subsequence of~$\{u_i\}$, we can assume that the sequence $\{z_j^k\}_{j\in{\mathbb Z}^+}$ converges to some $z^k\!\in\!\Sigma$ for every $k\!=\!1,\ldots,N$. \ 
oindent By~(ef{EnerPres3_e9}) and the ellipticity of the $ ar\partial$-operator, a subsequence of~$u_i$ converges uniformly in the $C^{\infty}$-topology on compact subsets of~$\Sigma_1^*$ to a $J$-holomorphic map \hbox{$v_1\!:\Sigma_1^*\!\longrightarrow\!X$}. By~(ef{EnerPres3_e9}) and the ellipticity of the $ ar\partial$-operator, a subsequence of this subsequence in turn converges uniformly in the $C^{\infty}$-topology on compact subsets of~$\Sigma_2^*$ to a $J$-holomorphic map \hbox{$v_2\!:\Sigma_2^*\!\longrightarrow\!X$}. Continuing in this way, we obtain a subsequence of~$u_i$ converging uniformly in the $C^{\infty}$-topology on compact subsets of~$\Sigma_j^*$ to a $J$-holomorphic map \hbox{$v_j\!:\Sigma_j^*\!\longrightarrow\!X$} for every $j\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+$. The limiting maps satisfy $$v_j|_{\Sigma_j\cap\Sigma_{j'}^*}=v_{j'}|_{\Sigma_j^*\cap\Sigma_{j'}^*} \qquad orall~j,j'\!\in\!{\mathbb Z}^+\,.$$ Thus, the~map $$u\!:\Sigma^*\!\equiv\!\Sigma^*\!-\! ig\{z^k ig\}\longrightarrow X, \qquad u(z)=v_j(z)~~ orall\,z\!\in\!\Sigma_j^*, $$ is well-defined and $J$-holomorphic.\ 
oindent By construction, the final subsequence of $u_i$ converges uniformly in the $C^{\infty}$-topology on compact subsets of~$\Sigma^*$ to~$u$. This implies~that $$E_g(u)\le \liminf_{i\longrightarrow\infty}E_g(u_i)=E\,.$$ By Proposition~ef{RemSing_prp}, $u$ thus extends to a $J$-holomorphic map $\Sigma\!\longrightarrow\!X$.
